# General coding standards

For **where** to put page-local vs app-wide code (components, `src/types`, `src/interfaces`, `src/constants`, `src/hooks`, `src/hooks/api/<domain>/`, `src/features/<feature>/`), see the project’s [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) at the repository root. **`type`** definitions live under `src/types`; **`interface`** declarations live under `src/interfaces` (two separate folders).

Under **`src/features/<feature>/components/`** and **`src/features/<feature>/providers/`**, use **one folder per** component or provider; the module file sits inside that folder (e.g. **`src/features/auth/providers/auth-provider/auth-provider.component.tsx`**, **`src/features/auth/components/require-auth-gate/require-auth-gate.component.tsx`**). **Higher-order components** live under **`src/features/<feature>/components/HOCS/<hoc-name>/`** (e.g. **`src/features/auth/components/HOCS/with-auth/with-auth.hoc.tsx`**). **`QueryClientProviderComponent`** (TanStack Query) lives under **`src/features/query/providers/`** (same one-folder-per-module pattern when multiple files exist there). Folder placement and other layout rules are in that doc.

For reusable libraries under `lib/`, prefer a local `README.md` when usage is not obvious from the exports alone.

**App Router API routes (`app/**/route.ts`):** Compose handlers with **`createRouteHandler`** from `@/lib/http/create-route-handler.util` and optional **`TRouteMiddleware`** using **`next()`** (see [lib/http/README.md](../../lib/http/README.md)). Shared types and `createRouteHandler` live under **`lib/http/`**. **`withMongoDbConnection`** and **`createGlobalRouteHandler`** live under **`app/api/_shared/route-handlers/`**; **`withRouteErrorHandler`**, **`AppError`**, **`appErrorResponseService`**, and **`jsonErrorBody`** live under **`app/api/_shared/features/error-handling/`** (`middlewares/`, `instances/`, `services/`, `utils/`). Shared **`APP_ERROR_CODES_TYPE`**, snackbar enums, and **`ISnackbarArgs`** live under **`src/features/error-handling/`**. The global handler wraps `createRouteHandler` with error handling + DB connection. For **intentional** HTTP errors (message + status for the client), **`throw new AppError({ … })`**, or **`BadRequestError`** / **`NotFoundError`** from the same **`instances/`** folder for fixed **400** / **404** responses; a bare **`Error`** caught by **`withRouteErrorHandler`** is turned into a generic **500** body (message hidden). Placement and full behavior: [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) (HTTP route helpers).

